  "goodToKnow": "Der Notar (die Notarin) is a notary. Unlike in the US or UK, German notaries are fully qualified lawyers with an important role: property purchases, company formations and many wills must be done before a notary (notariell beurkundet). The notary reads the entire contract aloud at the appointment, which can take hours. Their fees are set by law and add about 1.5 percent to property costs. Plural: die Notare."
